---
import Service from '../../../layouts/Service.astro'
import { images } from '../../../data/images'

const img = images.vveHero
---

<Service
  locale="en"
  path="/en/vve-management/"
  altPath="/vve-beheer/"
  title="VvE Management Haarlemmermeer | DSC Living"
  description="Communal-area upkeep, window cleaning, garden and coordinated inspections under one contract, with a condition report built for your long-term maintenance plan."
  serviceType="VvE property management"
  h1="VvE management and cleaning for apartment buildings"
  lead="As a board member of a VvE, you're usually arranging communal-area upkeep through several separate suppliers. DSC Living brings cleaning, window cleaning, garden care and coordinated inspections under one contract, with a condition report you can use directly for your long-term maintenance plan (MJOP)."
  breadcrumbs={[{ label: 'Home', href: '/en/' }, { label: 'VvE management' }]}
  heroImage={{ src: img.src, alt: img.alt, note: img.note }}
  ctaLabel="Request a proposal"
>
  <h2 class="h2 mt-10 mb-4">What does VvE cleaning cost per apartment?</h2>
  <p class="body-copy mb-4">
    That depends on the number of apartments, the size of the communal areas, and how often you
    want cleaning and upkeep. We visit for a free audit of the building, discuss the board's
    priorities, and send a written proposal within two working days — including a per-apartment
    indication so it drops straight into your budget.
  </p>
  <p class="body-copy mb-4">
    Because cleaning, window cleaning, garden care and inspection coordination run under one
    agreement, the VvE receives one invoice instead of several from several suppliers — and the
    board has one point of contact instead of five.
  </p>

  <h2 class="h2 mt-10 mb-4">What counts as a communal area?</h2>
  <p class="body-copy mb-4">
    Entrance, stairwell, lift area, galleries, storage corridors, and any shared garden or car
    park — in short, everything that isn't part of an individual apartment but is used daily by
    every resident. We build a job sheet with the board: which space, how often, and to what
    standard.
  </p>
  <p class="body-copy mb-4">
    For communal window cleaning and shared garden maintenance we use the same permanent staff
    as our other services. Where any part is delivered by a vetted partner, the proposal says so.
  </p>

  <h2 class="h2 mt-10 mb-4">Inspections we coordinate</h2>
  <p class="body-copy mb-4">
    Fire safety, lift inspections, communal-area electrics — mandatory inspections each run on
    their own schedule with their own certifying body. We manage the calendar, make sure the
    right certified firm attends, and archive the certificate once the inspection is complete.
  </p>
  <p class="body-copy mb-4">
    We don't carry out these inspections ourselves — that's done by the certified firms
    licensed to. Our role is coordination: keeping the calendar, informing the board, and making
    sure the paperwork is in order when an insurer or inspector asks for it.
  </p>

  <h2 class="h2 mt-10 mb-4">Condition reporting for your MJOP</h2>
  <p class="body-copy mb-4">
    At every visit we record the condition of the communal areas — what needs attention now,
    what's due within the year, and what can reasonably wait, each with a cost indication. This
    reporting is built to feed directly into your long-term maintenance plan, rather than leaving
    the board to compile everything from scratch.
  </p>
  <p class="body-copy mb-4">
    That's the real difference from a one-off cleaning arrangement: you get not just a clean
    entrance, but a running record of the building's condition.
  </p>

  <h2 class="h2 mt-10 mb-4">A proposal for your AGM</h2>
  <p class="body-copy mb-4">
    Preparing for a general members' meeting? We put together a clear, written proposal you can
    put straight on the agenda — scope, frequency and a per-apartment cost indication, so members
    can see exactly what they're voting on.
  </p>
  <p class="body-copy">
    Everyone we send is employed by DSC Living, on a Dutch employment contract. Where a service is delivered by a vetted partner, we tell you before you book. Everyone is screened before their first visit. More on that is on our
    <a href="/en/safety/" class="text-accent hover:underline">safety and security</a> page. Also
    managing individual homes alongside the building? See our
    <a href="/en/residential/" class="text-accent hover:underline">residential services</a>.
  </p>
</Service>
